  "related_closed_5099": {
    "number": 5099,
    "author": "uhhgoat",
    "state": "closed",
    "merged": false,
    "summary": "## Summary\n\nArchive now handles IMAP accounts that do not expose an archive-capable folder. The backend returns a structured `needs_archive_folder` response instead of failing ambiguously, the UI prompts the user to create `Archive`, then retries the original archive action only after the user confirms. The archive action now removes messages from the local UI only after a real archive success, archive/all-mail views hide redundant Archive actions, and the Email folder list can be explicitly refreshed so newly created or provider-side folder changes do not stay hidden behind folder cache.\n\n",
    "comments": []
  }
}
